    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d767">

                <pb facs="1241" n="1227" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War 1939/1234: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-05T18:00:00+01:00">January 5, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 5—4:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>92. American interests, Germany. Department’s 3222, December 24.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d767-f1"/> Swiss note January 4 states Swiss Legation, Berlin,
                    reports Minister Albrecht of German Foreign Office stated December 31 not yet
                    able comment reports concerned. Legal Section, Foreign Office, has likewise been
                    unable to so far give consideration this matter. Appears for present to involve
                    only threats in field political propaganda <pb facs="1242" n="1228"
                        xml:id="pg1228"/> but not yet possible verify degree to which these press
                    radio statements correspond to attitude German authorities.</p>
                <p>Swiss promise revert subject receipt Berlin’s detailed report. Repeated to
                    London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
